# Background {#sec:background}

The mass-energy equivalence is stated in @eq:mass, and the tree in
@fig:tree illustrates the structure it applies to. Both are discussed
by [@knuth1984]. @sec:results carries this further.

![A hazel tree.](tree.png){#fig:tree}

$$
E = mc^2
$$ {#eq:mass}

# Results {#sec:results}

A second figure keeps the per-section counters honest: see @fig:leaf.
The second equation, @eq:energy, follows from @eq:mass, which
@sec:background introduced.

![A hazel leaf.](leaf.png){#fig:leaf}

$$
E_k = \frac{1}{2}mv^2
$$ {#eq:energy}

The measurements are in @tbl:yields.

| Parameter | Yield |
|:----------|------:|
| Water     |   1.4 |
| Nitrogen  |   0.8 |
: Measured yield per parameter {#tbl:yields}

The result agrees with [@lamport1986] and, taken together, with
[@knuth1984; @lamport1986].
